{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.QuToQou","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.QuToQou","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Basic"],"declarations":37,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qu_to_qou_riemann_hurwitz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qu_to_qou_riemann_hurwitz","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L149-L153","doc":"Property (4): the Riemann–Hurwitz branch-point identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qu_to_qou_chi_neg_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qu_to_qou_chi_neg_six","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L136-L147","doc":"On a surface with `χ(A) = -6`, the obstruction vanishes at levels `1, 2, 3, 6`\nand persists at every level `n` coprime to `6`: it is not perpetual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qu_to_qou_obstruction_persists_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qu_to_qou_obstruction_persists_iff","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L131-L134","doc":"Property (3): the level-`n` obstruction persists exactly when `n ∤ χ(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qu_to_qou_first_obstruction_eq_euler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qu_to_qou_first_obstruction_eq_euler","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L126-L129","doc":"Property (2): the first obstruction κ₀ equals the Euler class χ(A). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qu_to_qou_descent_terminates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qu_to_qou_descent_terminates","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L121-L124","doc":"Property (1): the geometric descent terminates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qu_to_qou_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qu_to_qou_exists","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L96-L119","doc":"The five structural properties package into a QOU: given descent,\nobstruction, branch and terminal-fibre data satisfying their coherences,\nthey assemble into a `QuToQou`, and the assembled structure carries the\nsupplied descent and branch data. This formalises the *packaging* of the\nQU→QOU theorem (Properties 1–5); the derivation of these ingredients from\na quantum universe with observability and the quantum lifting condition is\nthe narrative content of §3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou.terminalFibers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou.terminalFibers","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L94-L94","doc":"(5) Terminal fiber data at each branch point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou.branchData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou.branchData","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L92-L92","doc":"(4) Branch point formula (Riemann–Hurwitz). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou.kummer_persistence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou.kummer_persistence","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou.kappa_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou.kappa_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou.kappa","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L88-L88","doc":"(3) Kummer persistence (degree condition): the level-`n` obstruction\nvanishes exactly when `n` divides `χ(A)`. Restated 2026-11-15 (owner\ndecision, PR #7747, bean `qou-lx8f`); the former field\n`perpetual : κ₀ ≠ 0 → ∀ n, κₙ ≠ 0` is false on Bring's surface, where\n`κₙ = 0` for `n ∈ {1, 2, 3, 6}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou.trace_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou.trace_map","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L82-L82","doc":"κ₀ maps to χ(A) under the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The Euler characteristic χ(A). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou.kappa_zero_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou.kappa_zero_obstruction","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L78-L78","doc":"(2) The first obstruction κ₀ is the Euler class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou.descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou.descent","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L76-L76","doc":"(1) The descent tower terminates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuToQou","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuToQou","kind":"structure","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L65-L94","doc":"The **main theorem**: packaging all five structural properties of a QOU.\n\nGiven a quantum universe (C, A, ω) with observability and the Yekutieli\nlifting condition, it is a QOU with descent, obstruction, and fiber data.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{thm:qu-to-qou}`\nRef: [leitner2026] §3 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TerminalFiber.involution_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TerminalFiber.involution_exists","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The involution σ : P(V) ↪ Ad(A) exists at this fiber.\nEncoded: the involution is an involution (σ² = id). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TerminalFiber.krull_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TerminalFiber.krull_zero","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The Krull dimension is 0 at the branch point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TerminalFiber.krullDimAtPoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TerminalFiber.krullDimAtPoint","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The Krull dimension at the branch point is 0 (discrete/Artinian).\nEncoded: the dimension of the descent tower at this point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TerminalFiber.branchIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TerminalFiber.branchIndex","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The branch point index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TerminalFiber.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TerminalFiber.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TerminalFiber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TerminalFiber","kind":"structure","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L52-L63","doc":"**Terminal fiber data** at a branch point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BranchData.riemann_hurwitz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BranchData.riemann_hurwitz","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The Riemann–Hurwitz identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BranchData.totalRamification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BranchData.totalRamification","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Total ramification R_tot = 2d + |χ(A)| (Riemann–Hurwitz). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BranchData.numBranchPoints","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BranchData.numBranchPoints","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Number of branch points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BranchData.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BranchData.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Euler characteristic χ(A) = tr(id_A). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BranchData.degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BranchData.degree","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Degree of the branched covering π : S → P(V). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BranchData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BranchData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BranchData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BranchData","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L39-L50","doc":"**Branch point data** from the Riemann–Hurwitz formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentTower.terminates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentTower.terminates","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Termination: dimension reaches 0 in at most krullDim steps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentTower.strict_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentTower.strict_descent","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L35-L35","doc":"Each step strictly reduces dimension (observability ⇒ faithful action). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentTower.initial_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentTower.initial_dim","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Initial dimension equals Krull dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentTower.dimAtStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentTower.dimAtStep","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L31-L31","doc":"The dimension at step n of the descent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentTower.krullDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentTower.krullDim","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Krull dimension of the centre Z(End_C(A)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentTower.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentTower.mk","kind":"ctor","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L27-L27","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentTower","kind":"structure","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/qu-to-qou.lean#L25-L37","doc":"**Descent tower data**: the geometric descent terminates in finitely\nmany steps, bounded by the Krull dimension. ","signatureChunk":0}]}